    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>#TEO_0000066</IRI>
        <Literal>Observed only by federal government employees in Washington, D.C., and the border counties of Maryland and Virginia, in order to relieve congestion that occurs with this major event. Swearing-in of President of the United States and Vice President of the United States. Celebrated every fourth year. Note: Takes place on January 21 if the 20th is a Sunday (although the President is still privately inaugurated on the 20th). If Inauguration Day falls on a Saturday, the preceding Friday is not a federal holiday.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
